{"name":"Wild Currant","hex":"#7c3239","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"wild","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Untamed; not domesticated.","Especially, being of the wild type: being of an unbroken ancestral line of undomesticated animals, as opposed to being feral, being an undomesticated animal whose ancestors were domesticated."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["Inaccurately; not on target.","Intended to be synchronized with film or video but recorded separately."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wild"},{"term":"currant","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A small dried grape, usually the Black Corinth grape.","The fruit of various shrubs of the genus Ribes, white, black or red."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/currant"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ribes","blocks":[{"text":"Ribes is a genus of approximately 200 known species of flowering plants, predominantly native to the temperate regions of the Northern Hemisphere. Ribes is the sole genus in the plant family Grossulariaceae. The genus includes species commonly referred to as redcurrants, blackcurrants, whitecurrants, and gooseberries. Several species are cultivated both for their edible fruit and as ornamental plants in horticulture. Ribes are the main alternate host for white pine blister rust, a fungal pathogen impacting five-needle pines."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Ribes_divaricatum_5391.JPG/330px-Ribes_divaricatum_5391.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ribes","wikidata":"Q22691"},{"title":"Zante currant","blocks":[{"text":"Zante currants, Corinth raisins, Corinthian raisins or simply currants, are raisins of the small, sweet, seedless grape cultivar Black Corinth. The name comes from the Anglo-French phrase \"raisins de Corinthe\" and the Ionian island of Zakynthos (Zante), which was once the major producer and exporter. It is not related to black, red or white currants, which are berries of shrubs in the genus Ribes and not usually prepared in dried form."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Grape_Rasins_plus_Zante_Currants.jpg/330px-Grape_Rasins_plus_Zante_Currants.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zante_currant","wikidata":"Q1382423"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/Schwarze_Johannisbeeren.jpg/500px-Schwarze_Johannisbeeren.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/Schwarze_Johannisbeeren.jpg/1280px-Schwarze_Johannisbeeren.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/Schwarze_Johannisbeeren.jpg/500px-Schwarze_Johannisbeeren.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Blackcurrant (Ribes nigrum)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASchwarze_Johannisbeeren.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Ribes_rubrum_a1.jpg/500px-Ribes_rubrum_a1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Ribes_rubrum_a1.jpg/500px-Ribes_rubrum_a1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Redcurrant (Ribes rubrum)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARibes_rubrum_a1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/Grossulariaceae_Fuchsia_flowered_Gooseberry_Ribes_speciosum.jpg/500px-Grossulariaceae_Fuchsia_flowered_Gooseberry_Ribes_speciosum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/Grossulariaceae_Fuchsia_flowered_Gooseberry_Ribes_speciosum.jpg/1280px-Grossulariaceae_Fuchsia_flowered_Gooseberry_Ribes_speciosum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/Grossulariaceae_Fuchsia_flowered_Gooseberry_Ribes_speciosum.jpg/500px-Grossulariaceae_Fuchsia_flowered_Gooseberry_Ribes_speciosum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Ribes speciosum (fuchsia-flowered gooseberry)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGrossulariaceae_Fuchsia_flowered_Gooseberry_Ribes_speciosum.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/Zante_currant_drying_in_Tsilivi.jpg/500px-Zante_currant_drying_in_Tsilivi.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/Zante_currant_drying_in_Tsilivi.jpg/500px-Zante_currant_drying_in_Tsilivi.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Sun-drying Zante currants on Zakynthos, with the grape vineyard in the background","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AZante_currant_drying_in_Tsilivi.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/Eccles_cakes.jpg/500px-Eccles_cakes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/Eccles_cakes.jpg/1280px-Eccles_cakes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/Eccles_cakes.jpg/500px-Eccles_cakes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Eccles cakes","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEccles_cakes.jpg"}],"sounds":{"wild":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/4a/En-us-wild.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=r